    "discardedPrototype": "The early version cached normalized clip tables. Whole-layout desktop medians rose in several cases. The selected source uses local scalars and keeps no clip tables.",
    "limits": "Desktop operation counts and clock samples are distinct from native frame timing. The roster fixtures exercise layout geometry rather than the real event cascade."
  },
  "preservation": [
    "The compiler only admits the precheck for its own compiled public geometry and the current fallback cell.",
    "Touching triangles still reach clipping. Strictly disjoint triangles contribute neither geometry nor a per-triangle empty cache entry.",
    "Standalone geometry guards, real intersections, fresh native material, existing visibility fallbacks and triangle limits keep their existing paths.",
    "Archived dense cases match all visible fields after geometric movement and again when the keeper hides. Desktop replays cover private material, clip boundaries, rollback and source recovery. Eighteen direct clip checks compare equal, touching and disjoint bounds in both styles."
  ],
